{
  "Ezra.10.24.5-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.13, number: 9 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 10:24.5</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 10:24.5</h1>\n  <h2>Remove dagesh from shin. Add note 't'</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.13/9-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The shin has only a very faint hint of a dagesh. (The shin-dot is not clear either.) The shin will be transcribed without the dagesh and a note 't' added.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh in the shin.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.13-9\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.13-9</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.2.42.8-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.13, number: 1 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 2:42.8</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 2:42.8</h1>\n  <h2>Examine fourth letter, a probable vav.  Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.13/1-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The fourth letter has only its top in ink. A clear shadow of a vav is present, however.  This might be an erasure or might be an unintentional loss of ink, e.g., flaking off. The transcription assumes the loss of ink on the vav was unintentional and keeps the vav. This is assumption agrees with Dotan's BHL. A transcription note 't' is added to reflect the uncertainty of the decision, however.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a vav as the fourth letter.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.13-1\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.13-1</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.3.3.11-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 39 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 3:3.11</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 3:3.11</h1>\n  <h2>Remove unsupported dagesh from last vav; place a qubuts under lamed in qere word. Add note 'q'. [וַיַּעֲל֨וּ]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/39-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere word in the right margin ends in a vav not present in the ketiv body text. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThe ketiv body text has a qadma and a qubuts on the lamed; no dagesh is available for the final vav. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThe UXLC retains the qubuts on the lamed to be true to the LC image. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tA transcription note 'q' is added to emphasize this decision.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh (acting as a shuruq dot) in the final vav, וַיַּעֲל֨וּ, for the qere word. BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-39\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-39</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.3.5.1-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.13, number: 2 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 3:5.1</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 3:5.1</h1>\n  <h2>Examine vowel below the resh and for possible splitting of word after the yod. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.13/2-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The text is of good quality. Three dots appear in a horizontal line under the resh; the first two are in contact. This is probably poor penmanship. No maqaf is apparent between the yod and the kaf. Word gaps are hard to judge and no gap is obvious between the yod and the kaf. Splitting the word at the yod without a maqaf leaves the first part of the word without an accent, however. Adding note 't'.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a tsere below the resh; it has a maqaf after the yod, starting a new word, כן.  BHLA has a tsere below the resh; it has a space after the yod, starting a new word, כן.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.13-2\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.13-2</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.4.11.8-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 22 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 4:11.8</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 4:11.8</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir aleph)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/22-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir note is in the right margin; it is a yatir aleph. The word on the line has a Masorah circle and two alephs. The first of these alephs is vowelized. The 'y' note will be added to the second aleph. WLC 4.20 lacks a 'y' transcription note for this word.</p>\n  <p>BHL has no qere/ketiv pair for this word; the word starts and ends with an aleph.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-22\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-22</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.4.12.15-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 23 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 4:12.15</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 4:12.15</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir aleph) Add 't' note for ambiguity.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/23-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is the left margin; it is a yatir aleph. The word has a Masorah circle and contains two alephs; the first has an unexpected rafe mark, the second, final aleph, is accented. The first aleph will be marked as the yatir. Add a 't' note to indicate ambiguity.</p>\n  <p>BHL has no qere/ketiv pair for this word; both alephs are retained.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-23\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-23</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.4.12.15-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 23 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 4:12.15</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 4:12.15</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir aleph) Add 't' note for ambiguity.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/23-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is the left margin; it is a yatir aleph. The word has a Masorah circle and contains two alephs; the first has an unexpected rafe mark, the second, final aleph, is accented. The first aleph will be marked as the yatir. Add a 't' note to indicate ambiguity.</p>\n  <p>BHL has no qere/ketiv pair for this word; both alephs are retained.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-23\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-23</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.4.14.11-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2021.12.02, number: 2 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 4:14.11</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 4:14.11</h1>\n  <h2>Word lacks a maqaf so that it has no primary accent. Add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes/images/2021.12.02/2-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                    The lack of a maqaf on this word means the it has no primary accent.\n                    Instead, it has two metegs, an unusual marking.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n                    The digital text correctly represents the LC which has no maqaf.\n                </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Ben Denckla</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes/2022.04.01 - Changes.xml?2021.12.02-2\">2022.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2021.12.02-2</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.6.2.9-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.13, number: 4 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 6:2.9</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 6:2.9</h1>\n  <h2>Examine sheva below vav. Add dagesh to vav. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.13/4-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The upper dot of the putative sheva under the vav is very weak, but well-positioned. A very clear dagesh is present in the vav, however.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a sheva below the vav.  BHLA has a sheva below the vav; however, it has a dagesh in the vav.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.13-4\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.13-4</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.7.18.3-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 24 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 7:18.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 7:18.3</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/24-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is the left margin; it is a yatir yod. </p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere word haS no yod.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-24\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-24</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.7.18.6-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 25 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 7:18.6</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 7:18.6</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/25-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is the left margin; it is a yatir yod. </p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere word lacks a yod.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-25\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-25</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.7.20.6-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.13, number: 5 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 7:20.6</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 7:20.6</h1>\n  <h2>Examine first letter. Change vowel under the pe to patah.  Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.13/5-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The text is in poor condition, with much chipping of ink. (The image shows the final yod of the previous word.)  The outline of a chipped yod at the start of this word is evident. The vowel below the pe could be a patah, a segol, or qamats. The shape of the upper portion of the vowel is more like a broken bar than two dots; this would make the vowel either a patah or qamats.  The lower portion of the vowel appears to be an erasure, rather than chipping, as the shape of the area is too large to be a chipped dot. The vowel will be transcribed as a patah and a note 't' added.</p>\n  <p>BHL has an initial yod and a segol under the pe.  BHLA has an initial yod and a qamats under the pe.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.13-5\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.13-5</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Ezra.8.25.1-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 26 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Ezra 8:25.1</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Ezra 8:25.1</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir vav)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/26-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is the left margin; it is a yatir vav.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere word lacks a vav.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-26\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-26</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>"
}
